 "notes": "PRIMARY SOURCE: official Niagara Parks 2023 Ussher's Creek scorecard PDF (operator's own card). CROSS-CHECK 1: the official 2022 Niagara Parks Ussher's Creek card reproduces every per-hole yardage, par and both handicap rows identically for Gold/Blue/White/White-Green/Green; it predates the Blue/White combo tee, which appears only on the 2023 card. CROSS-CHECK 2: Hole19 independently matches all 18 pars and all 18 men's stroke indexes exactly. ARITHMETIC: every tee's OUT, IN and TOTAL were recomputed from the per-hole yardages and match the printed totals exactly; the men's and ladies' handicap rows are each a complete permutation of 1-18 (odds on the front, evens on the back). 'handicap' is the MEN'S stroke index; 'handicapLadies' is the ladies' row. TEE NAMES: printed on the card as GOLD, BLUE, BLUE WHITE, WHITE, WHITE GREEN, GREEN. Blue/White and White/Green are combination tees (a mix of the adjacent tee decks), separately rated. DISCREPANCIES: (a) the 2022 card lists the White/Green ladies' slope as 129, the 2023 card as 133 - the 2023 value is used here; (b) the 2022 card publishes no ladies' rating for the Gold tee ('-'), the 2023 card gives 81.4/150. All other rating/slope values agree between the two cards. NOT BATTLEFIELD: verified against the official Battlefield card (7309 yds Gold, par sequence 5-4-3-4-4-5-4-3-4), which shares no numbers with this one. Chippawa is the facility's separate nine. Rating/slope are Golf Canada men's and ladies' values as printed. All distances measured to centre of green."
}